{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:dependence-heldout-reviewer-fable-14", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:6f1702f1e1ff3855d34f", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "Every k1 code (ha01–ha24) and every k2 code (hb01–hb24) appears exactly once across the 24 staged rows, so each source unit contributes exactly one measurement to the procedure.", "observed_value": "24 distinct k1 codes and 24 distinct k2 codes over 24 rows; no repetitions", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "ha01,hb13,ht01,401.0,402.0\nha02,hb14,ht02,401.5,402.25"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "ha24,hb12,ht24,412.5,412.25"}]}, {"description": "The reported df=46 equals 24+24-2, consistent with one entry per distinct unit in each collection rather than inflated repetition.", "observed_value": "df=46.0", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] TtestResult(statistic=np.float64(-0.8581613266497022), pvalue=np.float64(0.3952529117073811), df=np.float64(46.0))"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The workflow does use a row-independent procedure (independent-samples t-test), so the issue class would be in play if any unit code were repeated; this precondition alone is met but repetition is absent.", "observed_value": "st.ttest_ind applied to all rows", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "result = st.ttest_ind(left, right)"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to demonstrate the issue by searching the 24 rows for any duplicated k1 or k2 identifier; ha01 through ha24 and hb01 through hb24 each occur exactly once. I also checked whether the reported degrees of freedom implied more entries than distinct units; df=46 matches 24 unique units per collection. Both checks failed to produce the issue, so the not-demonstrated verdict stands.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:75bb533785f478cbdd8d", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task explicitly withholds any claim that k1 or k2 identifies a source item, so equal code values cannot be read as repeated entries of the same measured unit.", "observed_value": "codes declared opaque; unit identity not established", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Treat `k1` and `k2` as opaque codes; `tag` is an opaque annotation. This task does not establish whether either code identifies a source item within either collection."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Each k1 code value appears twice (ma01–ma06 each on two rows) and all rows feed a row-independent independent-samples t-test, which would demonstrate the issue if those codes identified source units.", "observed_value": "each ma code appears on 2 of 12 rows; ttest_ind used", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "ma01,mb07,mt01,501.0,502.0\nma01,mb11,mt02,502.0,504.0"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "result = st.ttest_ind(left, right)"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to demonstrate the issue via the visibly repeated ma-codes feeding ttest_ind. This fails because the issue class requires repeated entry of the same independent source unit, and the task file expressly states the codes are opaque and do not establish that either code identifies a source item. Treating repeated opaque codes as repeated units would be guessing an unstated intention, which the review protocol forbids. The disclaimer is explicit rather than ambiguous, so I record a within-scope non-demonstration rather than an unresolved question.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "medium"}, {"case_id": "case:8a68d6ae147ce49e2a11", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "Each first-collection source unit ea01–ea12, which the task states is identified by k1 and measured by column a, appears on exactly two staged rows, and the workflow feeds all 24 resulting a-values into scipy's independent-samples t-test, a procedure that treats every entry as an independent observation; the report's df=46 confirms all repeated unit entries were counted as independent, so the same authorized unit was repeatedly entered into a row-independent procedure.", "root_cause": "The workflow passes every row's a-value directly into st.ttest_ind without aggregating or deduplicating by the k1 unit identifier, so the two measurements per ea-unit are counted as two independent observations, inflating the effective sample size of the first collection from 12 units to 24 entries.", "issue_class": "issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task establishes that k1 identifies a first-collection source item measured by column a.", "observed_value": "k1 = source-unit identifier for column a", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "`k1` identifies a first-collection source item measured by column `a`"}]}, {"description": "The same k1 unit appears on multiple rows: ea01 occurs on two consecutive rows with two different a-values, and this two-rows-per-unit pattern runs through ea12.", "observed_value": "12 distinct ea units across 24 rows, each contributing 2 a-values", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "ea01,eb07,et01,101.0,102.0\nea01,eb08,et02,101.5,102.25"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 24, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "ea12,eb05,et23,112.0,112.0\nea12,eb06,et24,112.5,112.25"}]}, {"description": "All row-level a-values are fed unaggregated into an independent-samples t-test, which assumes each entry is an independent observation.", "observed_value": "st.ttest_ind over 24 left entries from 12 units", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "left = [float(row[\"a\"]) for row in staged]\nright = [float(row[\"b\"]) for row in staged]\nresult = st.ttest_ind(left, right)"}]}, {"description": "The selected report shows df=46 (24+24-2), confirming the duplicated unit entries were counted as independent observations in the produced result.", "observed_value": "df=46.0", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] TtestResult(statistic=np.float64(-0.8581613266497022), pvalue=np.float64(0.3952529117073811), df=np.float64(46.0))"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task instructs applying the procedure to the complete staged row sequence, which could be read as authorizing entry of every row as-is; however, this authorizes the rows as input, not treating repeated measurements of one declared unit as independent observations.", "observed_value": "instruction to use complete row sequence", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Apply the named procedure to the complete staged row sequence."}]}, {"description": "The k2 codes (eb01–eb24) are all distinct, so the second collection's entries are not repeated; the issue is demonstrated only on the k1 side.", "observed_value": "24 distinct eb codes", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 2, "quoted_text": "ea01,eb07,et01,101.0,102.0"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "ea12,eb06,et24,112.5,112.25"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify by (1) checking whether equal ea codes could denote different units — the task states k1 identifies a source item and provides no basis for splitting equal codes into distinct units; (2) checking whether the procedure accounts for repetition — st.ttest_ind has no grouping mechanism and the reported df=46 proves all 24 entries per side were treated as independent; and (3) checking whether the disclaimer that row pairing is a storage convention removes the problem — it addresses cross-column pairing, not within-column repetition of the same unit. All falsification routes failed, so the demonstrated verdict stands.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:a516621a9cc0c4f6854d", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "All 12 k1 codes (ca01–ca12) and all 12 k2 codes are distinct across the 12 staged rows, so each source unit enters the procedure exactly once.", "observed_value": "12 distinct k1 codes and 12 distinct k2 codes over 12 rows", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 2, "quoted_text": "ca01,cb07,ct01,201.0,202.0"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 13, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "ca12,cb05,ct12,212.0,212.0"}]}, {"description": "The reported df=22 equals 12+12-2, consistent with one entry per distinct unit in each collection.", "observed_value": "df=22.0", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] TtestResult(statistic=np.float64(-0.6793662204867575), pvalue=np.float64(0.5039915691282064), df=np.float64(22.0))"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The workflow uses a row-independent procedure (independent-samples t-test) on all rows, so the issue class would apply if any unit were repeated; that precondition is met but no repetition exists.", "observed_value": "st.ttest_ind applied to all rows", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "result = st.ttest_ind(left, right)"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to find duplicated identifiers among the 12 rows: ca01–ca12 each appear once and the cb codes (cb01,cb03,...,cb23 pattern) are pairwise distinct. I also verified the reported df=22 matches 12 distinct units per side, ruling out hidden entry inflation. No route to demonstrating the issue succeeded.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:c37ea6f502dc593de820", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "Each first-collection source unit r01–r08, which the task states is identified by k1 and measured by column a, appears on exactly three staged rows, and the workflow feeds all 24 resulting a-values into scipy's Mann-Whitney U test, a rank procedure that treats every entry as an independent observation; the same authorized units are therefore repeatedly entered into a row-independent procedure, with the reported U=288 arising from all 24 repeated entries per side.", "root_cause": "The workflow passes every row's a-value directly into st.mannwhitneyu without aggregating or deduplicating by the k1 unit identifier, so the three measurements per r-unit are ranked as three independent observations, inflating the effective first-collection sample from 8 units to 24 entries.", "issue_class": "issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task establishes that k1 identifies a first-collection source item measured by column a.", "observed_value": "k1 = source-unit identifier for column a", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "`k1` identifies a first-collection source item measured by column `a`"}]}, {"description": "The same k1 unit appears on multiple rows: r01 occurs on three consecutive rows with three different a-values, and this three-rows-per-unit pattern runs through r08.", "observed_value": "8 distinct r units across 24 rows, each contributing 3 a-values", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "r01,z09,q01,701.0,699.125\nr01,z10,q02,701.25,699.625\nr01,z11,q03,701.75,700.125"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "r08,z06,q22,708.0,709.625\nr08,z07,q23,708.25,710.125\nr08,z01,q24,708.75,710.625"}]}, {"description": "All row-level a-values are fed unaggregated into a Mann-Whitney U test, which assumes each ranked entry is an independent observation.", "observed_value": "st.mannwhitneyu over 24 left entries from 8 units", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "left = [float(row[\"a\"]) for row in staged]\nright = [float(row[\"b\"]) for row in staged]\nresult = st.mannwhitneyu(left, right)"}]}, {"description": "The selected report's U statistic of 288 is exactly half of 24×24=576, consistent with all 24 entries per side (including the repeated unit entries) being ranked in the produced result.", "observed_value": "statistic=288.0, pvalue=1.0", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] MannwhitneyuResult(statistic=np.float64(288.0), pvalue=np.float64(1.0))"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task instructs applying the procedure to the complete staged row sequence, which could be read as authorizing every row's entry; however, this authorizes the rows as input, not treating three measurements of one declared unit as three independent observations.", "observed_value": "instruction to use complete row sequence", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Apply the named procedure to the complete staged row sequence."}]}, {"description": "The k2 codes (z01–z24) are all distinct, so the second collection's entries are not repeated; the issue is demonstrated only on the k1 side.", "observed_value": "24 distinct z codes", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 2, "quoted_text": "r01,z09,q01,701.0,699.125"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "r08,z01,q24,708.75,710.625"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify by (1) checking whether equal r codes could denote distinct units — the task states k1 identifies a source item, giving no basis for that reading; (2) checking whether Mann-Whitney has any mechanism to handle clustered or repeated entries — it does not, and the U=288 value is consistent with 24 entries per side all being ranked; and (3) checking whether the storage-convention disclaimer covers within-column repetition — it only disclaims cross-column row pairing. The demonstrated verdict survived all three attempts.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:c41c53bc6fedd68b0ccc", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "All 12 k1 codes (pa01–pa12) and all 12 k2 codes are distinct across the 12 staged rows, so no source unit is entered more than once.", "observed_value": "12 distinct k1 codes and 12 distinct k2 codes over 12 rows", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 2, "quoted_text": "pa01,pb05,pt01,601.0,603.0"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 13, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "pa12,pb03,pt12,612.0,613.0"}]}, {"description": "The procedure applied is a paired (related-samples) t-test, which is not a row-independent procedure; the in-scope issue class requires repeated unit entry into a procedure that treats rows as independent.", "observed_value": "st.ttest_rel used", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "result = st.ttest_rel(left, right)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The workflow imposes row pairing via ttest_rel even though the task states row pairing is a storage convention with no relationship between the paired items; this is a serious methodological problem, but it is a fabricated-pairing/dependence-assumption concern, not repeated entry of an independent unit into a row-independent procedure, and is therefore outside the scope of this review.", "observed_value": "paired test applied to unrelated items; df=11 and p=1.6e-05 reflect the fabricated pairing", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "The row pairing is a storage convention only; there is no matching, pairing, block, or other relationship between the `k1` item and the `k2` item in that row."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] TtestResult(statistic=np.float64(-7.26636084983398), pvalue=np.float64(1.610229916816512e-05), df=np.int64(11))"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to demonstrate the in-scope issue two ways: (1) searching for repeated k1 or k2 identifiers — pa01–pa12 and the pb codes are all distinct, so no unit is repeatedly entered; and (2) considering whether the ttest_rel misuse could be recast as this issue class — it cannot, because the defect there is assuming a within-row relationship the task denies, not repeated entry of one unit, and ttest_rel is not a row-independent procedure. Per the review protocol, this out-of-scope concern must not be recorded as the in-scope issue class.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:e9e6bf9e80c9287dabe5", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "All 12 k1 codes (va01–va12) and all 12 k2 codes are distinct across the 12 staged rows, so each source unit contributes exactly one entry to the procedure.", "observed_value": "12 distinct k1 codes and 12 distinct k2 codes over 12 rows", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 2, "quoted_text": "va01,vb04,vt01,301.0,303.0"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 13, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "va12,vb02,vt12,312.0,313.0"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The workflow uses a row-independent rank procedure (Mann-Whitney U) on all rows, so the issue class would apply if any unit code were repeated; that precondition is met but no repetition exists.", "observed_value": "st.mannwhitneyu applied to all rows", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "result = st.mannwhitneyu(left, right)"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to find any duplicated identifier: va01–va12 each appear once, and the vb codes (vb04, vb06, ..., vb24, vb02) are pairwise distinct. I also checked the reported U=50 for consistency with 12 entries per side (maximum U would be 144), which raises no sign of entry inflation. No route to demonstrating repeated unit entry succeeded, so the not-demonstrated verdict stands.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}